1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:06,005
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:08,925 --> 00:00:10,427
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

3
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:12,637
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

4
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:16,224
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

5
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,226
Didn't I tell you

6
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:19,352
that's the losers' club?

7
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:22,188
I told you we’re not losers.

8
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:24,274
We are Earth Savers!

9
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:26,568
It's getting hard for me to
lie to Audrey too.

10
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:27,402
Attorney!

11
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:30,280
Colonel Mercado left a
property in your name.

12
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:31,990
Boss left you an inheritance?

13
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:34,451
Do you want to sleep over at our house

14
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:35,785
this weekend?

15
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:37,871
Hailey: Then we'll practice in the room.

16
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,330
Janine: Where's the speaker?

17
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:40,749
Hailey: I gave it to you earlier, right?

18
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:42,584
Janine: Wait.
Maybe I left it in the restroom.

19
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:43,626
[thuds]
[clatters]

20
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:46,254
You took our speaker?!

21
00:00:46,337 --> 00:00:47,297
Ibyang: I was going
to return it immediately.

22
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,047
Gross!

23
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:49,424
[glass shattering]

24
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:50,717
Students: Oh no!

25
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,719
You broke the mirror!

26
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:55,096
The mirror is broken!

27
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,139
Elias: This looks familiar.

28
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:58,183
San Antonio de Padua.

29
00:00:58,266 --> 00:01:00,602
Shugo: Sir, that saint has the same
name as Atoy, right?

30
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:01,186
[weapon swooshes]

31
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:04,230
[clangs]

32
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:05,398
[groans]

33
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:07,108
[music continues]

34
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:08,485
Son of a thread.

35
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:09,778
Sir Atoy.

36
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:10,487
Uno?

37
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:12,781
What exactly happened to you, huh?

38
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:15,450
Why is that Samir so furious at you?

39
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:16,493
What did you do?

40
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:19,662
Uno: Belladonna, she's the last mission

41
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:21,623
Sir Mercado gave me.

42
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:23,291
[gunshots]

43
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:26,336
[music continues]

44
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:29,088
Uno: The Agency will protect you.

45
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:30,048
Let's move,

46
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:31,007
before they catch up with us.

47
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:31,800
That's the reason

48
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:35,345
Obsidian came home
to the Philippines, huh?

49
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:36,387
Probably.

50
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:38,223
You should watch over them too!

51
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:41,810
Why-- why does it seem like you're
blaming me as if it's my fault?

52
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:43,812
That I'm not taking care of our children.

53
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:44,854
Where have you been, anyway?!

54
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,189
Cita: That's enough!

55
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:47,857
How will the kids make up,

56
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:50,652
if their parents are bickering too?!

57
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:51,986
Go on, tell me!

58
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:56,866
[crickets chirping in the distance]

59
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:08,128
[pensive music playing]

60
00:02:09,462 --> 00:02:10,964
[door lock clicks]

61
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:15,260
[music continues]

62
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:22,225
[door closes]

63
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:25,770
[music continues]

64
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:39,492
Mmm-hmm.

65
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:43,413
I heard you fought again.

66
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:47,834
[music continues]

67
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:50,712
Oh, what now?

68
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,339
What happened this time?

69
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:55,425
[soft drama music playing]

70
00:02:56,718 --> 00:02:58,303
So, what will happen to…

71
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,680
Ibyang Thread?

72
00:03:00,763 --> 00:03:03,141
What will happen to Janine Needle?

73
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:06,185
Daddy, please tell Ibyang

74
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:07,437
that what she did was wrong.

75
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:09,689
I don't understand her.

76
00:03:09,772 --> 00:03:11,649
She used to be so nice,

77
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,651
and now she's becoming a bully.

78
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:15,153
Atoy: Is that so?

79
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:18,698
Ahh, well.

80
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:20,658
Oh, Ibyang…

81
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:24,245
Janine says you should--

82
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:25,747
Tatoy…

83
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:29,417
please tell Janine that I'm not a bully,

84
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,920
and I was going
to return it too, you know.

85
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:33,379
Oh?

86
00:03:33,463 --> 00:03:35,256
It's just that she caught me.

87
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:42,388
Janine, oh, Ibyang said--

88
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:45,141
Why did she even take the speaker, Daddy?

89
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,226
If she's mad at me,

90
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:48,102
she could have just talked to me.

91
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:51,064
That's not hard to understand.

92
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:52,649
That's true.

93
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:56,444
Ibyang, Ibyang, well, if you took--

94
00:03:56,527 --> 00:03:57,987
Well, it's because of Janine,

95
00:03:58,071 --> 00:03:59,781
how can I even talk to her?

96
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:01,908
She's always with Hailey.

97
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:05,161
Even at recess they eat together.

98
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:07,789
And they just keep practicing the dance.

99
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:09,499
Practicing the dance.

100
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:12,460
Oh, Janine, then?

101
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:13,836
- She said--
- Because, Daddy…

102
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:16,631
We just want to be good.

103
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:18,800
We just want to--

104
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:21,135
Well, you know, we want to prove that…

105
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,681
we can join the dance club.

106
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:25,265
Hmm?

107
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:26,766
Well, wait.

108
00:04:26,849 --> 00:04:28,268
Why don't you just face each other?

109
00:04:28,351 --> 00:04:29,978
Why don't the two of you talk?

110
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:34,857
Well, Tatoy, Janine is good at dancing.

111
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:36,359
But I wish…

112
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:39,320
she had time for me too.

113
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:41,364
Because…

114
00:04:43,157 --> 00:04:45,118
I miss her.

115
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,494
Why don't you just face each other?

116
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:49,539
Tell her directly what you feel.

117
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:53,418
I don't want to.
Her head might get bigger.

118
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:55,837
[music fades]

119
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:57,255
What?

120
00:04:58,673 --> 00:04:59,924
Is it true?

121
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:00,842
You missed me?

122
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:04,012
Let me test that.

123
00:05:04,762 --> 00:05:05,638
Let me test that!

124
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:07,348
Ouch. Ow, ow. Stop--

125
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:08,558
[giggles]

126
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:10,852
There, there, look! There.

127
00:05:10,935 --> 00:05:11,519
[giggles]

128
00:05:11,602 --> 00:05:13,271
Oh, oh, oh! Wait!

129
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:15,481
What? Are you two okay now?

130
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:16,983
Are you both okay now?

131
00:05:17,608 --> 00:05:19,444
Huh? I hope you two are okay now,

132
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:22,113
so I won't get in trouble with your mommy.

133
00:05:22,196 --> 00:05:23,239
Are you both okay now?

134
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:24,073
[sentimental music playing]

135
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:25,825
It doesn't look like it! Aargh!

136
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:26,951
[giggles & exclaims]

137
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,203
Huh? Huh, huh, huh?
[giggles]

138
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:32,415
It’s okay now.

139
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,500
They've made up.

140
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:36,919
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

141
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:40,590
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

142
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:44,385
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

143
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,471
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

144
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:47,847
♪ The hole in my polo

145
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:49,849
that's right under the armpit ♪

146
00:05:49,932 --> 00:05:52,101
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

147
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:53,853
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

148
00:05:53,936 --> 00:05:55,813
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

149
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:59,358
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

150
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,611
[gunshots]

151
00:06:01,694 --> 00:06:03,362
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

152
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:05,323
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

153
00:06:05,948 --> 00:06:06,866
[music swells]

154
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:10,578
[music fades]

155
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:13,164
Atoy: Come here.

156
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:17,210
[footsteps approaching]

157
00:06:19,504 --> 00:06:21,130
Oh, you have something
to say to your mommy.

158
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:24,258
Sorry, Mommy.

159
00:06:25,384 --> 00:06:27,345
Ibyang and I won't fight anymore.

160
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:30,932
And sorry about…

161
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:34,268
the broken things at school.

162
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:36,854
It won't happen again.

163
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,356
Are you sure about that?

164
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:40,608
Are you both okay now?

165
00:06:41,317 --> 00:06:42,401
- Yes.
- Have you made up?

166
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:45,196
It's true.

167
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:48,074
I witnessed them talk.

168
00:06:48,157 --> 00:06:49,534
That's good,

169
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:52,370
because we'll join this!

170
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:55,373
There's a family day at school,

171
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:57,917
and I think it will be a good bonding
activity

172
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,920
for us if we join the competition.

173
00:07:01,003 --> 00:07:03,464
- Atoy: Oh! Oh!
- What? Game?

174
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:04,048
Game!

175
00:07:04,423 --> 00:07:05,424
I'm game!

176
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:06,384
- Will you join?
- Oh, how about you, Tatoy?

177
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:07,760
Well! Of course,

178
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,053
and in that competition,

179
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:11,055
there's no Team Lose, no Team Win.

180
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:13,808
We only have Team Padua!

181
00:07:13,891 --> 00:07:14,600
Whoa!

182
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:15,768
For the win!

183
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:16,477
Atoy: For the win?

184
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:17,854
I'm excited!

185
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:19,981
Excited, excited!

186
00:07:20,064 --> 00:07:23,234
You can't miss that day, okay.

187
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:25,403
Of course. I got this.

188
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,738
Oh, win on three!

189
00:07:28,322 --> 00:07:29,907
1, 2, 3…

190
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,993
All: Win!

191
00:07:33,786 --> 00:07:37,665
Love, I'm sorry for what I said earlier.

192
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:40,126
Ah, I promise you, next time

193
00:07:40,209 --> 00:07:42,253
I'll choose my words better.

194
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:46,841
I also made a mistake.

195
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:48,968
I shouldn't have blamed you.

196
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:52,305
I was just so stressed because…

197
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:56,517
those two were even arguing
in front of the principal.

198
00:07:56,601 --> 00:07:57,935
So embarrassing!

199
00:07:58,019 --> 00:08:00,104
Yes, that’s true. Let it go.

200
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:00,771
[clicks tongue]

201
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:01,772
I know something, though…

202
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,484
to relieve your stress.

203
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,277
[light music playing]

204
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:08,362
Hmm? Hmm?

205
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:11,073
What? What?

206
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,075
Uhm… [clears throat]

207
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:14,994
[giggles]

208
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:18,998
Hey, sorry.

209
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:20,333
[Audrey clears throat]

210
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:23,711
Oka, why just now?

211
00:08:25,129 --> 00:08:26,923
I was given a last-minute errand by…

212
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:28,549
Baks.

213
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:30,134
- Atoy: Baks?
- Hey.

214
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:32,595
Don't say that at the office, okay.

215
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:34,889
He'll hear you, you'll be in trouble.

216
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:37,391
Why? Does he know he's the Baks

217
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:38,809
we're talking about?

218
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:40,102
Audrey, you know--

219
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:41,145
Audrey: Hey!

220
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:43,397
That's enough!
[Oscar laughs]

221
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:45,608
Later. Okay, that's it.

222
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:46,776
I'll leave you two.

223
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:47,527
Bye, Love. I'm going up.

224
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:48,528
Yes, okay. Good night.

225
00:08:49,153 --> 00:08:50,238
Don't snitch on me, okay!

226
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:52,573
[chuckles]

227
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:55,243
[pensive music playing]

228
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:56,035
Okay, ah.

229
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,788
I'm glad you and Audrey are getting close.

230
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:00,289
Really, buddy?

231
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:00,915
Atoy: Yes.

232
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:03,626
Well, you even have inside jokes

233
00:09:03,709 --> 00:09:04,293
about Baks.

234
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:05,419
Well, who-- who is Baks anyway?

235
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:06,546
Oscar: Secret!
[both chuckle]

236
00:09:06,629 --> 00:09:08,339
Ah, is that so? [chuckles]

237
00:09:08,422 --> 00:09:09,924
Atoy: Well, well, that's good.

238
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:12,426
Well, thank you for being there for her.

239
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:14,095
So you can also keep an eye on her,

240
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:16,180
in case anyone is lurking around.

241
00:09:17,056 --> 00:09:18,057
You can take care of it.

242
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:18,891
That's automatic.

243
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:19,559
Atoy: Yes.

244
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:20,893
'Toy, don't worry.

245
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:21,894
I'll take care of Audrey.

246
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:23,396
Thank you.

247
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:26,566
I love her too.

248
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:27,149
[heavy music playing]

249
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:28,526
[titters]

250
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:29,318
Ah, what did you say?

251
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:30,736
As family!

252
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:31,821
Family, right?

253
00:09:31,904 --> 00:09:32,738
Atoy: Ah!

254
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:34,448
You're like my brother so…

255
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:36,409
I consider Audrey family too.

256
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:38,703
Even the girls, the kids.

257
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:39,537
You know…

258
00:09:40,037 --> 00:09:41,080
I'll take care of them too,

259
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:42,039
just like you do.

260
00:09:43,082 --> 00:09:43,666
[clicks tongue]

261
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:45,835
Thank you, buddy.

262
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:47,878
I appreciate it.

263
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:49,338
[chuckles]

264
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:49,922
Baks, huh.

265
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:50,548
[chuckles]

266
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:53,926
Baks, when you see him, you'll know.

267
00:09:54,677 --> 00:09:55,595
[chuckles]

268
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,889
[music fades]

269
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:03,519
Ah, Oka, wish me luck.

270
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:06,355
I'll present a budget proposal later to…

271
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:08,649
Baks.

272
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:10,610
[chuckles]

273
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:12,486
You of all people?

274
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:13,487
You don’t even need luck.

275
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:14,864
You can totally do it.

276
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:17,325
Lord, I hope he's okay.

277
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:19,243
Please, please.

278
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:20,328
[Jona gasping]

279
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:21,621
Ms. Audrey!

280
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:22,496
- Oh, Jona?
- Ms. Audrey!

281
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,415
Jona: It’s Boss! He collapsed.

282
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,042
Where is he?!

283
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:29,337
P-A-D-U-A!

284
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,964
♪ Padua! Padua! We’ll win for sure! ♪

285
00:10:32,048 --> 00:10:32,715
[chuckles & applauds]

286
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:33,466
Ame: Wow! Great job, ah!

287
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:36,302
[lively chatter]

288
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:37,470
Oh, Tatoy!

289
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:40,890
Help us with our cheer for family day.

290
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:43,726
Yes, so we can win best in cheer.

291
00:10:43,809 --> 00:10:44,602
Best.

292
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:45,978
Well, what you did looks good already!

293
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:47,438
Okay?

294
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:49,774
But there’s still something lacking.

295
00:10:50,274 --> 00:10:51,567
Daddy, come on. Please!

296
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:53,110
- Help us out.
- Atoy: Still lacking?

297
00:10:53,819 --> 00:10:55,613
Ah, I'm sorry--

298
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:57,156
I have an errand.

299
00:10:57,239 --> 00:10:57,865
I need to leave already.

300
00:10:57,948 --> 00:10:58,699
Cita: Atoy…

301
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:00,534
your children rarely make a request.

302
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:01,702
Just give in this time.

303
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:03,913
- Come on, Tatoy.
- Come on.

304
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:04,789
Please?

305
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:07,583
Cita: Where are you going for real?

306
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:10,795
Huh?

307
00:11:11,295 --> 00:11:12,713
Answer me.

308
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:14,757
What errand is so much more important

309
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,050
than your children?

310
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:17,343
Where are you really going?

311
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:21,472
[soft drama music playing]

312
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,268
[music fades]

313
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,979
Audrey: Eh, eh-- have you
called an ambulance?

314
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:29,939
Jona: I already called, Ms. Audrey.

315
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:31,148
They're on their way.

316
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:32,733
Audrey: What exactly happened?

317
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,236
He was supposed to meet with the weavers.

318
00:11:35,319 --> 00:11:36,904
Then he walked to his table.

319
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:39,532
And then he just suddenly collapsed.

320
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,952
Well, do you have Sir's emergency contact?

321
00:11:43,452 --> 00:11:44,662
Let's call his family.

322
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:45,246
Okay.

323
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:47,623
Audrey, the ambulance needs
to get here now.

324
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:48,874
He has no pulse.

325
00:11:53,295 --> 00:11:56,340
[foreboding music playing]

326
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:05,558
[ambulance stretcher clattering]

327
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:09,937
Once his family arrives from Bicol,

328
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:12,857
that's when we'll coordinate their…

329
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,233
final decisions.

330
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:17,945
Of course, they were shocked too by…

331
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,738
how fast it happened.

332
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:21,907
But they'll be here as soon as possible.

333
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:23,576
Thank you, Ma'am.

334
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:24,869
Just update us.

335
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:26,328
Thank you.

336
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,675
Oka, uhm…

337
00:12:40,968 --> 00:12:42,470
Where’s Jona?

338
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:45,598
Um, she's inside.

339
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:49,602
With the people who were supposed
to meet Mr. Tinio.

340
00:12:49,685 --> 00:12:51,479
[music continues]

341
00:12:51,979 --> 00:12:53,063
Audrey, how about you?

342
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:54,690
How are you?

343
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:01,238
Not okay, actually.

344
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:08,120
You know, even though Sir
has that kind of attitude…

345
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:12,917
I never wished that…

346
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:15,085
he would die.

347
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:17,755
[melancholic music playing]

348
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:20,508
It just reminded me of when…

349
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:23,344
my dad died.

350
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:26,388
[music continues]

351
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:28,933
I wasn't even able to take care of him.

352
00:13:29,517 --> 00:13:31,185
Audrey: You need
to be taken to the hospital.

353
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:32,186
[groans & gasps]

354
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:33,103
Dad!

355
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,813
Dad! Dad!

356
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:35,397
[groans]

357
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:36,106
[sobs]

358
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:37,525
Get out of here!

359
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:39,443
Audrey, run away!

360
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:41,987
I'm not leaving you and my daughter, Dad!

361
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:43,948
No! No!

362
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:45,324
[sobs]
[heavy breathing & sobbing]

363
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:46,325
No, Dad.

364
00:13:47,409 --> 00:13:49,286
Forgive me, my child,

365
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:52,998
for not telling you the truth and…

366
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,625
I'm sorry

367
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:56,794
that you grew up in this kind of life.

368
00:13:57,336 --> 00:13:59,713
I wasn't even able to attend his wake.

369
00:14:03,092 --> 00:14:05,511
[music continues]

370
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:07,137
It's-- it's complicated.

371
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:08,514
I can't really talk about it.

372
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:11,725
[music continues]

373
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:13,435
But my boss…

374
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:17,690
whom I don't even like that much…

375
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:22,820
I'm the one taking care of everything

376
00:14:24,321 --> 00:14:25,698
for him.

377
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:27,741
[music continues]

378
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:28,450
I just…

379
00:14:30,536 --> 00:14:32,663
I just find it so unfair.

380
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:36,667
[ominous music playing]

381
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:38,919
I understand you, Audrey.

382
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:45,467
[music swells]

383
00:15:02,735 --> 00:15:03,652
Tatoy!

384
00:15:03,736 --> 00:15:04,820
Mommy!

385
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:05,696
Ibyang!

386
00:15:05,779 --> 00:15:07,197
And Janine!

387
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:09,575
1, 2, 3, go!

388
00:15:09,658 --> 00:15:11,452
P-A-D-U-A!

389
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:12,328
The winner is--

390
00:15:12,411 --> 00:15:13,370
All: The winner is the family!

391
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:15,414
Team Padua wins!

392
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:16,999
Yay!

393
00:15:17,082 --> 00:15:20,002
That's it! That's it! Oh, ha.

394
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:22,129
[lively chatter]

395
00:15:22,212 --> 00:15:24,924
Team Padua is a winner for sure.

396
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,926
We just need to teach Mommy her part.

397
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:28,344
Your mommy can totally do that.

398
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:29,887
Your mommy is a dancer!

399
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:32,848
Thank you, Tatoy,

400
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:36,560
for helping us make the cheer.

401
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:37,728
Whoa!

402
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:39,313
Wow! You bet.

403
00:15:39,396 --> 00:15:41,190
[chuckles]

404
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:42,483
[light music playing]

405
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:47,154
[Atoy clears throat]

406
00:15:47,237 --> 00:15:48,948
[suspicious music playing]

407
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:57,581
Tatoy, Janine and I are okay now.

408
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,334
You can leave now.

409
00:16:00,417 --> 00:16:01,752
We’re okay now?

410
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:04,546
Don't forget what I taught you, okay.

411
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:05,381
Okay? All right.

412
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:06,715
Yes, Daddy.

413
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:07,675
[smooches]

414
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:08,300
Bye. Bye-bye.

415
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:09,635
Take care.

416
00:16:09,718 --> 00:16:10,427
Ame.

417
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:14,974
[theme music playing]

418
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:27,611
Ame, I'm going
to the tailoring shop first, okay.

419
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:28,946
You take care of the kids.

420
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:31,240
Yes. Just message me if you need me.

421
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:32,783
- Oh, okay. Okay.
- All right.

422
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:34,159
Siony: Miss Cita!

423
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,912
Siony, goodness, you’re very loud, huh.

424
00:16:36,996 --> 00:16:39,039
Well, someone is looking for you.

425
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:42,292
They're interested in buying your house.

426
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:43,293
Who are they?

427
00:16:43,377 --> 00:16:44,294
Well, I told them someone is still renting

428
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:45,587
but that you're the owner.

429
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:46,714
Who are they?

430
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:47,297
Siony: Ah--

431
00:16:52,052 --> 00:16:52,636
- Cita?
- Rudy?

432
00:16:54,221 --> 00:16:55,556
Well, do you two know each other?

433
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:58,475
Both: Yes.

434
00:16:59,143 --> 00:16:59,852
Ah…

435
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:01,603
Cita is my first love.

436
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:03,605
[sentimental music playing]

437
00:17:03,689 --> 00:17:04,898
First love.
[mouthing words]

438
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:06,275
What are you saying? Goodness.

439
00:17:06,358 --> 00:17:07,234
That was a long time ago.

440
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:08,736
[chuckles]

441
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:10,404
Oh, wow!

442
00:17:10,487 --> 00:17:13,657
Exes meeting again.

443
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:15,743
Siony: Brought together by fate!

444
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:16,452
[chuckles]

445
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:20,414
Cita, Rudy is apparently a widower.

446
00:17:20,497 --> 00:17:21,582
[exclaims, then giggles]

447
00:17:21,665 --> 00:17:23,876
[music continues]

448
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:26,837
You live here, Cita?

449
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:28,547
Ah, yes.

450
00:17:29,256 --> 00:17:30,424
Ah, temporarily.

451
00:17:30,507 --> 00:17:32,926
This is Atoy's house, my godson.

452
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,011
We're staying together for now

453
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:35,345
while another house is being repaired,

454
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:37,931
because I'm also planning to sell

455
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,308
our other house.

456
00:17:42,936 --> 00:17:45,564
Oh, so are you two just going to keep
staring at each other

457
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:47,900
or will you go to Manang
Cita's house now?

458
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:49,359
[sentimental music playing]

459
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:50,486
Both: Ah…

460
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:52,279
Right.

461
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:53,363
Right. Oh, well--

462
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:54,406
Okay, we'll leave now.

463
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:55,866
Both: Let's go.

464
00:17:57,993 --> 00:18:01,497
[music continues]

465
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:03,874
Thank you.

466
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,209
Ms. Audrey…

467
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:07,002
Oh, are you okay?

468
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:09,630
Um, I'm going home now,

469
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:10,756
and I might also drop by

470
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:11,799
to see Father Peping

471
00:18:11,882 --> 00:18:14,551
because I'll request a Mass…

472
00:18:15,844 --> 00:18:17,137
for Boss.

473
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,180
Ah, thank you.

474
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:20,015
Take care.

475
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:21,934
Bye, Ms. Audrey.

476
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:26,855
Ah, how about you?
Are you okay?

477
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:30,150
I'm sorry.

478
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:32,319
I know you only came here

479
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:32,986
for a meeting,

480
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:35,572
but this day turned out
to be traumatic for you.

481
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:40,035
Ah, would you like us to take you home?

482
00:18:40,702 --> 00:18:42,496
We won't refuse, Ms. Audrey.

483
00:18:42,579 --> 00:18:44,498
We're live quite far from here.

484
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:47,626
Thank you, Ms. Audrey.

485
00:18:47,709 --> 00:18:48,752
Oh, it's nothing.

486
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:50,796
At least that way

487
00:18:50,879 --> 00:18:53,340
we can make it up to you
for coming here.

488
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:55,717
Oka.

489
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:59,179
Please prepare the service.

490
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:01,723
Um, where are we going?

491
00:19:02,766 --> 00:19:05,310
Antipolo, Weavers Haven.

492
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:14,945
[music fades]

493
00:19:18,615 --> 00:19:22,494
[suspicious music playing]

494
00:19:33,797 --> 00:19:35,090
What are you looking for?

495
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:39,803
I'm looking for a, uh, person here.

496
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:43,932
[music swells]

497
00:19:45,517 --> 00:19:48,312
Look for the directress of Weavers Haven,

498
00:19:48,395 --> 00:19:51,398
and present your profile card to her.

499
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:54,109
Uno: So that she'll trust you.

500
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:58,030
But she'll ask you a safety question.

501
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:00,073
What's your favorite flower?

502
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:02,075
And your answer…

503
00:20:03,076 --> 00:20:04,620
is another name for Belladonna.

504
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:06,705
Nightshade.

505
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:09,166
[suspicious music playing]

506
00:20:09,249 --> 00:20:11,543
You're looking for Beatriz Davos?

507
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:13,837
She's no longer here.

508
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:16,882
[music continues]

509
00:20:16,965 --> 00:20:18,717
Do you know where she went?

510
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:20,427
No, I don't.

511
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,429
She left without saying goodbye.

512
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:26,058
Directress: It was obvious
she was in a hurry.

513
00:20:26,141 --> 00:20:27,851
She left some belongings.

514
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:29,603
We haven't put them away yet.

515
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:31,897
[tense music playing]

516
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:34,149
May I see her room?

517
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:36,151
[music swells]

518
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:55,545
[suspicious music playing]

519
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:08,558
[music swells]

520
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:13,897
Weaver: Excuse me!

521
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:16,525
[speaking in Visayan]
What are you taking from there?

522
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:18,527
Atoy: Ah.

523
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:21,363
Well, I just feel it's a waste of paper.

524
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:22,864
Hmm?

525
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:25,075
Ah, do you know the one…

526
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:26,576
who sleeps there,

527
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,912
the one in this room?

528
00:21:29,454 --> 00:21:30,330
Weaver: Of course!

529
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,748
She's my BFF here.

530
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:32,958
[speaks in Visayan]
Really?

531
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:36,211
you know where she went.

532
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:37,296
Really?

533
00:21:37,379 --> 00:21:38,672
But I miss her too, you know.

534
00:21:38,755 --> 00:21:40,590
She was only here for
almost two weeks.

535
00:21:41,216 --> 00:21:42,342
Ahh.

536
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,053
Oh, okay.

537
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:47,014
Well, thank you very much!

538
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:48,307
Okay.

539
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,683
Why do you have
so many questions, by the way?

540
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:51,435
[speaking in Visayan]
Are you related to her?

541
00:21:51,518 --> 00:21:52,227
Hey!

542
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:53,478
Are you her boyfriend?!

543
00:21:53,562 --> 00:21:55,564
Please take a look inside too, Ms. Audrey.

544
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:57,607
Our rooms were also newly renovated.

545
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:58,608
Oh, okay.

546
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:01,486
Weaver 2: Yes. They're in the
work room now.

547
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:02,154
Weaver 1: Yes.

548
00:22:02,237 --> 00:22:03,155
Ah, can you introduce me

549
00:22:03,238 --> 00:22:03,822
to the other staff.

550
00:22:03,905 --> 00:22:05,574
- Okay, sure. Come.
- So it won't be hard for me.

551
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:06,658
Audrey?

552
00:22:06,742 --> 00:22:09,578
[tense music playing]

553
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:10,912
Buddy.

554
00:22:10,996 --> 00:22:12,122
Atoy?

555
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:13,999
[music continues]

556
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,293
What are you doing here?

557
00:22:19,838 --> 00:22:21,131
[music swells]

558
00:22:21,214 --> 00:22:25,052
[electronic blipping]

559
00:22:25,135 --> 00:22:30,932
[intense music playing]

560
00:22:31,016 --> 00:22:34,019
Is this you, tracker 307, the Firefighter?

561
00:22:34,102 --> 00:22:35,020
Belladonna,

562
00:22:35,103 --> 00:22:37,314
there's another tracker who…

563
00:22:37,397 --> 00:22:39,066
needs to talk to you.

564
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:41,151
Wait for me wherever you are,

565
00:22:41,234 --> 00:22:43,445
I only trust Tracker 307.

566
00:22:43,528 --> 00:22:44,738
You won't catch me here.

567
00:22:44,821 --> 00:22:46,907
All I ask is for you to trust me.

568
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,325
What kind of client is that, huh?

569
00:22:48,408 --> 00:22:50,160
Why is it needed right away?

570
00:22:50,243 --> 00:22:52,037
Oh, fine. Well, I'll just call.

571
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,622
I'll tell them we'll reschedule.

572
00:22:53,705 --> 00:22:54,998
But not tomorrow, okay.

573
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:56,750
It's the kids' family day!

574
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,919
Emerson: Atoy, Samir's man is here,

575
00:22:59,002 --> 00:23:00,629
the mestizo one, the one
who looks like you.

576
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:01,963
[theme music playing]

577
00:23:02,047 --> 00:23:03,173
Where's Belladonna now?

578
00:23:04,508 --> 00:23:05,926
[gunshot]
[groans]

579
00:23:06,009 --> 00:23:08,011
Man: We need you, Belladonna.

580
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:09,805
Save her.

581
00:23:11,556 --> 00:23:14,643
["Mamang Sastre" playing]
